rssync:entry:bb5ab186676d413db75cf62c4ddfecd13c6ba46ceed030a663526ff2ea2e5f95</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T16:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tim-curry-of-the-rocky-horror-picture-show-dies-at-80/a-78514945--42aea1d6e079.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tim-curry-of-the-rocky-horror-picture-show-dies-at-80/a-78514945?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The gender-bending role as Dr. Frank-N-Furter put Curry on the map in 1975. He then went on to play a number of villainous roles like Gomez Addams, Pennywise and Bill Sikes, but also Mozart and William Shakespeare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Reports: UEFA backs off FIFA boycott threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26db6e67eaac145867be8e949423f8a09b10adce3473cf057323305ba4b06c7d</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T13:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/reports-uefa-backs-off-fifa-boycott-threat/a-78511519--372fe96c45a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/reports-uefa-backs-off-fifa-boycott-threat/a-78511519?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">UEFA is reportedly set to withdraw a threat to boycott FIFA tournaments over a plan to partially privatize football tournaments. The Under-20 Women's World Cup is to be hosted by Poland next month.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gamescom 2026: What's next for the gaming industry?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a73a09e4ed61d8f76b4401bd29b37834c9f47e8611d6a914a7abcee005c7fdce</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849--a4d043f1bdf6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gamescom-2026-what-s-next-for-the-gaming-industry/a-78502849?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Gamescom 2026 opens in Cologne, AI, hardware costs and slowing user growth are putting pressure on the global games industry despite its current strength.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Remembering Dolly Parton: 8 facts about the icon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:186bbbb8c65a7bca67dff7a84f3c02c8f18e156874838df9e9694d20c1538375</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/remembering-dolly-parton-8-facts-about-the-icon/a-75503168--5fa1e70ed52f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/remembering-dolly-parton-8-facts-about-the-icon/a-75503168?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dolly Parton, one of the world's most successful artists, has died at the age of 80. Here are some important and extraordinary facts about the country music superstar.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>US country music legend Dolly Parton dies aged 80</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5597785e86397904a179282dedcdf30f7f1ad6112eee13f3c8a5780b05398c</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-country-music-legend-dolly-parton-dies-aged-80/a-78501931--2eb06224b286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-country-music-legend-dolly-parton-dies-aged-80/a-78501931?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Representatives of the country music legend told US media that Dolly Parton died after a "brief battle with cancer." Parton's career spans more than half a century and includes a wide array of smash hits.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Schalke coach looks to Bosnia bond in Bundesliga return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94e14205e7fd470f622ffbe58034a0a333cf65383e3b6e1a1dcec0dd43d4d165</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/schalke-coach-looks-to-bosnia-bond-in-bundesliga-return/a-78486008--84b6333f3a23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/schalke-coach-looks-to-bosnia-bond-in-bundesliga-return/a-78486008?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After three seasons in the second division, Schalke are back in the Bundesliga. Just a year ago, few would have guessed that their revival would largely be 'Made in Bosnia.'</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's Volkswagen could cut 100,000 jobs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca061e0d8c09a9e09a26c0b40f89f20f2c0a4877775f439f5cb54328d81dab0b</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715--3ad4df2f83bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-volkswagen-could-cut-100-000-jobs/a-78483715?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Europe's biggest automaker, Volkswagen, faces Chinese competition, high costs and US tariffs. What could its restructuring mean for the German car industry?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Can new US sanctions cripple Iran's shadow economy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9a8fe826fc79c12b1e1df6a3e66a2faead6e4dbc023562f4a29137b7eacdb2</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630--d793d396bd52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-us-sanctions-cripple-iran-s-shadow-economy/a-78494630?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is expanding sanctions on Iran's financial networks, targeting crypto, gold, aviation and shipping. DW spoke with analysts about what could change.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Trees are vital for cooler cities, but they need help too</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80d5194fcf3ee9db81a59a603f0212971be4b2c49655a014a424df07eff6a34e</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trees-are-vital-for-cooler-cities-but-they-need-help-too/a-78488665--39588bf2d5df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trees-are-vital-for-cooler-cities-but-they-need-help-too/a-78488665?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record-breaking heat and drought are putting urban trees at risk. Experts explain how to protect these essential assets and build city forests that can withstand the climate challenges ahead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>The new Bundesliga season is here, but has the glow gone?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c2ec3c137fcdd262cd88960e8018777df3b454fdcbc3ff0eed21ce975c81b8a</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T14:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032--f578ab52d735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-new-bundesliga-season-is-here-but-has-the-glow-gone/a-78062032?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Another Bundesliga season arrives, but are the golden years of Germany's top football league already over, and what can it do to change its course?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Star violinist Anne-Sophie Mutter: 50 years on stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a52dd63affe757ba4d02d2eda9f16e5f518477e6d4df0c82ae9e095301cf4d4a</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T11:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/star-violinist-anne-sophie-mutter-50-years-on-stage/a-78484739--30785cb37716.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/star-violinist-anne-sophie-mutter-50-years-on-stage/a-78484739?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anne-Sophie Mutter constantly reinvents herself. For her 50th onstage anniversary, the star violinist is surprising audiences with sounds from around the world and never-before-recorded commissions.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Scientists discover new 'immune hubs' in skull bone marrow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aad229c1feef2488b411ae99f147337f091e170362bca31abd4c836f68037281</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-new-immune-hubs-in-skull-bone-marrow/a-78460417--3ae7f2c7a79f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/scientists-discover-new-immune-hubs-in-skull-bone-marrow/a-78460417?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">"Immune hubs" that actively defend the brain have been discovered in mouse skull marrow. Similar cells exist in human skulls, but their role remains unclear.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Spiraling health costs force Iranians to delay care</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dfc2dd7823bb96ad16677f0c3c5caab0f996ff8d81a1b8f1575d7d64d148e65</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-24T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430--f9e115d582df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spiraling-health-costs-force-iranians-to-delay-care/a-78455430?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A single chemotherapy session in Iran can cost six times the monthly minimum wage. As drug prices soar and medicine is in short supply, doctors say more patients are delaying or abandoning treatment.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Sydney Marathon medal wrongly shows German landmark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc655bd2feb40ec8e961b13eb628bdb39b70a3985e9c5c5f113a749666258128</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-23T06:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sydney-marathon-medal-wrongly-shows-german-landmark/a-78473705--c4d12c38e946.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sydney-marathon-medal-wrongly-shows-german-landmark/a-78473705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A medal minted for finishers in the Sydney Marathon features a skyline of the city — with one landmark from rather far away. Organizers say the muddle only makes the medal "a little more unique."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Germany's gas storage levels are so low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:410c329f739cda1dc0ade31dda3f25c3d933915ca3d9dd932402a6c41a77482b</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T14:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677--5b5bdc8c00df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-germany-s-gas-storage-levels-are-so-low/a-78440677?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's gas storage facilities are only 50% full as traders bet that wholesale prices will fall if the Iran war ends. With around three months until winter, DW asks whether the country can refill its reserves in time.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>How Europe can better protect against extreme wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:144b7e0239fd1d7748ef7e2ff91f30350e33b0a91b89c94213d93aebdb74cf6d</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243--a1a3032b9e1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-europe-can-better-protect-against-extreme-wildfires/a-78435243?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In another summer of European wildfires that have even seen wetlands burning, scientists say the situation is set to worsen in the future. What's needed is fire prevention and climate protection.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Evergrande founder Hui Ka Yan sentenced to life in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03d06af47f122ca27ead9918f2ba84aab9dcd597f6db1b549f725639aad0a8ee</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-20T07:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153--ba088f0f4c18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evergrande-founder-hui-ka-yan-sentenced-to-life-in-prison/a-78439153?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese court ordered the former billionaire's assets to be confiscated and fined Evergrande-related companies billions of dollars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>In drought-stricken France, tankers supply drinking water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15c90cb406b621946b812ace10f1c4194a9bc9d9921665cd362c7e2e5f1e4fe9</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-drought-stricken-france-tankers-supply-drinking-water/a-78420016--bd4077809bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-drought-stricken-france-tankers-supply-drinking-water/a-78420016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France is seeing water shortages in regions that usually have plenty of supply. This summer's extreme heat is exposing how unprepared much of the country, and Europe, is for increasing water scarcity.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How to grow food for more people in a hotter world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50f32171e261efab0fb5d0c3d7d95fe7d4996f5e63cce7ed51ed8db1f3f76b98</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-to-grow-food-for-more-people-in-a-hotter-world/a-78413324--6e9042895db0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-to-grow-food-for-more-people-in-a-hotter-world/a-78413324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Inside futuristic labs, plants are scanned, stressed and analyzed. The aim is to use the results to produce plant strains that can better serve a growing population in a warming world.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Do not inhale! How wildfire smoke 'affects the whole body'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e8dc852957d496ce7d2533246b4e1e2bbdfcd13be0c9be3419b3b5a1e455cb3</id><updated>2026-09-16T19:36:42Z</updated><published>2026-08-18T08:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/do-not-inhale-how-wildfire-smoke-affects-the-whole-body/a-76039654--04a98638c5fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/do-not-inhale-how-wildfire-smoke-affects-the-whole-body/a-76039654?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Wildfires destroy lives and livelihoods. But survivors and firefighters also suffer long-term harm to their health. A growing body of research suggests particulate matter (PM2.5) in wildfire smoke is a major culprit.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry></feed>
